      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Simplify $-(-4b)^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(-4b)^{3} & = \\\\ -((-4)^{3}\\cdot {b}^{3}) & = \\\\ -(-64{b}^{3}) & = \\\\ 64{b}^{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
