      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${({a}^{-1}b)}^{-7}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({a}^{-1}b)}^{-7} & = \\\\ {({a}^{-1})}^{-7}{(b)}^{-7} & = \\\\ {a}^{(-1)(-7)}\\cdot {b}^{-7} & = \\\\ {a}^{7}\\cdot {b}^{-7} & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}^{7}}{{b}^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
