      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${({x}^{-2}{y}^{6})}^{-2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({x}^{-2}{y}^{6})}^{-2} & = \\\\ {({x}^{-2})}^{-2}{({y}^{6})}^{-2} & = \\\\ {x}^{(-2)(-2)}\\cdot {y}^{(6)(-2)} & = \\\\ {x}^{4}{y}^{-12} & = \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{{y}^{12}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
