      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "${(5w{z}^{-5})}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(5w{z}^{-5})}^{2} & = \\\\ {5}^{2}\\cdot {w}^{2}\\cdot {({z}^{-5})}^{2} & = \\\\ {5}^{2}\\cdot {w}^{2}\\cdot {z}^{-5\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ 25\\cdot {w}^{2}\\cdot {z}^{-10} & = \\\\ \\frac{25{w}^{2}}{{z}^{10}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
